      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Every setting, in one place\n\n| Setting | What it does | Ours |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Steps** | How many passes. Fewer is faster and rougher | **16** |\n| **CFG** | How hard it obeys the prompt | **2** |\n| **Sampler** | The maths that removes the noise | **euler** |\n| **Scheduler** | How the work is spread across the steps | **simple** |\n| **Shift** | Nudges contrast and framing. It does more at low step counts than high ones | **3** |\n| **Denoise (2)** | How much of your own picture survives | **0.55** |\n| **Size** | Portrait suits this model. Squares are not what it is for | **960 x 1440** |\n| **LoRA** | Ships switched OFF so the first run needs nothing extra | **off** |\n\nThis is the one model where **CFG** and the **negative prompt** actually do something. That is\nthe whole difference between this file and the Turbo one, and it is why it is slower.\n\n### Want the pro version\nThree models, a detail pass and a real upscale, all in one file on switches. It is not sold\non its own — it comes with the Krea 2 course, and you get the file when you finish it.\n**stableyogi.com**"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
